stments to yield benefits. Introducing richer data without model co-optimization can initially reduce performance.\n*   **Focus on Core Levers:** Filter capacity is the dominant factor for spectral pattern recognition, more critical than architectural intricacies. Diminishing returns are observed beyond a sweet spot (~128 filters). Multi-scale feature extraction is beneficial but requires careful balance to avoid introducing instability without proportional gains.\n*   **Trust Conservative Metrics:** Validation loss is the most reliable compass for optimization. Aggressive training approaches with faster convergence are negatively correlated with final accuracy; slower, more stable training with moderate learning rates produces superior results.",
